(I have submitted this to the development team.)

Synopsis:

    Trolls can reach experience level 0.

Steps to reproduce:

     1) In wizard mode, create a chaotic character on dungeon
        level 1.
     2) #levelchange to experience level 30.
     3) Wish for and wear extreme armor protection (e.g., +128
        dragon scale mail).
     4) Wish for a stethoscope.
     5) Wish for and wield the -10 Stormbringer. (The idea is to
        cause level drain without inflicting much physical damaage.)
     6) Wish for and apply a cursed Olog-hai figurine.
     7) Hit the Olog-hai until you see a message about Stormbringer
        reducing the Olog-hai's level.
     8) Using the stethoscope, monitor the Olog-hai's HP, and wait
        until the HP are back to maximum.
     9) Repeat steps 7 and 8 until the Olog-hai reaches experience
        level 1.
    10) Hit the Olog-hai again. If it lives, the stethoscope will show
        it to be at experience level 0. If it dies, wait for it to
        ressurect -- it will then be at experience level 0.

    This pattern is true for all troll types. I just find the problem
    easiest to reproduce with Olog-hai.

    Sometimes the Olog-hai will start with low HP relative to its
    experience level. In that case you may have to restart with
    Step 6 and hope for a more robust Olog-hai.

Suggested fix:

    Unless experience level 0 is really supposed to exist in the
    game, trolls should die when at level 1 and level drained,
    and should then resurrect at level 1.

